{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>and my heart was secretly enticed</b> — like: פן יפתה לבבכם (lest your heart be enticed)." "<b>and my mouth kissed my hand</b> — one of the kinds of idolatry, for most of the ancients, before the prophets came, used to worship the two luminaries. Therefore he said: for this too is an iniquity deserving of judgment, for I denied El above — and the meaning is that He is above the luminaries."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:09.957882778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}